  filter is exact-match only, so it fetches unfiltered and narrows\n214\t  client-side — and carries them through `ConversationSummary.events` in\n215\t  seq order; `turnCount` still counts only visible turns.\n216\t  `src/targets/codex.ts`'s `buildRolloutLines` replays each reasoning\n217\t  event's verbatim `raw.data` response_item line at its correct seq position\n218\t  when `event.producer.source === \"codex\"` — gated per-event, not\n219\t  per-conversation, even though today's data model (a `ConversationSummary`\n220\t  groups by one native session id, hence one source) makes that equivalent\n221\t  to a per-conversation check in practice; genuine multi-hop carry-over\n222\t  (reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning via the lineage chain when\n223\t  re-bridging) is deliberately not built and stays a follow-up. Never\n224\t  applies to a Claude Code target: foreign reasoning can't be forged as a\n225\t  native reasoning item, so the only real switch is whether provider-matched\n226\t  replay happens, not what it's coerced into — unreadable/foreign reasoning\n227\t  is still folded into labeled text as before. On by default (decided\n228\t  2026-07-23); opt out with `--no-reasoning-replay` or\n229\t  `{\"reasoningReplay\": false}` in `~/.turnbridge/config.json` (`src/config.ts`).\n230\t  No ownership gate — replay applies to any synced conversation, not just\n231\t  the current user's own, per 2026-07-23 decision. The fabricated session's\n232\t  import notice (`buildRolloutLines`) is conditional: it discloses the\n233\t  replayed-block count when replay happened instead of the blanket \"hidden\n234\t  reasoning ... not transferred\" claim, and still states that claim for\n235\t  everything else in the same session. Empirically verified via\n236\t  scripts/probe-encrypted-reasoning.mjs (manual injection, independent of\n237\t  this integration): same-account and cross-account replay of a real blob in\n238\t  a fabricated session is accepted across sessions, CLI versions, and a\n239\t  different paid ChatGPT account (identical token accounting), so the\n240\t  ciphertext is not keyed per-account; the free tier cannot run Codex at all.\n241\t  Still open: blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves the same\n242\t  as ChatGPT auth — turnbridge attempts replay unconditionally either way\n243\t  since auth mode isn't observable from here; a rejected blob at actual\n244\t  `codex resume` time has no proactive detection and falls under the same\n245\t  `--bootstrap` escape hatch as any other fabrication-drift failure.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fo3AxNhMBaEA1XTBJbrWfz","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","seq":40},"id":"ev1-afed07bb1dc097693b0dbbb85cafa4556136e17bf0af21fd158a6e324f78e90d","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T03:44:02.027Z","producer":{"session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"130\tthose turns under new event ids.\n131\t\n132\t## Risks\n133\t\n134\tNative formats change without notice (fabrication is version-pinned, bootstrap\n135\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (the ledger\n136\tredacts at capture and sync time, but matching is pattern/entropy-based and\n137\tcannot catch every secret — review before sharing still matters); full\n138\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n139\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n140\t\n141\t## Roadmap\n142\t\n143\tToward an npm releas