10387).** The reasoning is recorded in the workflow header and the roadmap, because the idea is tempting enough to recur:\n\nCI cannot validate a pin. The probes that earn one need both target CLIs installed, a TTY for the interactive smoke test, and paid model credentials per provider to make the recall turns real. So any PR CI opened would be a mechanical one-line bump with nothing behind it — saving a trivial edit while creating a *mergeable* artifact asserting a validation nobody performed. An issue cannot be merged, and that asymmetry is the whole argument. The agent-drafted variant (the old commented-out stage 2) fails identically: its blocker was never the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, it was the per-provider credentials the probes need.\n\nThe workflow is back to `permissions: contents: read` with no repo writes of any kind.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 77/77 tests pass\n- `node scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs` → exit 0, both targets validated\n=== checks ===\nGitGuardian Security Checks\tpass\t34s\thttps://dashboard.gitguardian.com\t\n=== files ===\n35+ 33- .github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml\n14+ 6- docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md\n35+ 1- docs/specs/codex-rollout-format.md\n2+ 2- package-lock.json\n1+ 1- package.json\n8+ 4- scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs\n2+ 1- scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs\n9+ 7- src/targets/codex.ts\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N6PEchweN159b72mVTq2p1","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342-afd7-bbadf34f59ee","seq":908},"id":"ev1-f6f963dcf58ae8bdfbb6e1f89daf548fa00bd027eeef4294fed1a7917d745db1","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T03:21:15.191Z","producer":{"session_id":"f6bb2ded-a3cb-4342